ust said that you actually got  better with age how do you explain that  i think it's just going about my career  doing all the right things on and off  the field from day one and never  switching off  not taking any shortcuts  doing the ice baths daily getting the  massages daily eating well hydrating  and just layering with my training you  know just constantly trying to get more  and more fit  and really just not putting limits on  myself and i think when you live a  healthy lifestyle you take care of  yourself and you don't switch off and  you just live and breathe this um  i mean there's there's no reason why i  wouldn't get better with age can i just  ask you about the psychological  component of this uh as well because you  know when you're in the public eye when  you're pro athlete you get a lot of  negative comments as you would expect  some people ignore them you opted as i  understand it to make a list of the  negative comments and save them and save  them yes  why do that i was wondering about that  too tony yeah just use it as fuel um i  you know i'm a jersey girl through and  through i i grew up just across the  bridge from philadelphia so you guys  know philly is a rough place to to be in  especially as a sports fan and  yeah i just use those to kind of  motivate me fuel me um i took note of  them and you know i remember kind of  reading this crazy article before the  2015 world cup that called me the  weirdest world-class athlete ever  took note of that and then went out and  scored a little hat trick in that final  there you go um  you know you gotta have tough skin  that's for sure but speaking of that you  know you played longer than me i played  11 years in the nfl prior to that caught  my first football at eight i know about  the long nights i know about the  injuries the physical ones but even more  so  the mental scars that we can't shake i  know about the world celebrating you  while you feel like you're in isolation  um the praise not gettin